7 kg, 63 kg\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor height: 160 cm, 160 cm\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor smoker: no, no\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor blood_type: O+, O+\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = anticoagulant: ACDA\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = source: STEMCELL technologies\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = description donor_sex: pooled: D1 - female, D2 - female\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = suspension type: cell\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor dev_stage: adult stage\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor living_at_sample_collection: TRUE\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor body_mass_index: pooled: D1 - 34, D2 - 24.6\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor disease: normal\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample preservation_method: formaldehyde fixed -80C\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor ethnicity: pooled: D1 - Hispanic or Latin American, D2 - African American\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genetic perturbation_strategy: CRISPR interference\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = crispr system_type: constitutive\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = suspension enriched_cell_types: CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = suspension depletion_factors: EasySep™ Human Naïve CD4+ T Cell Isolation Kit: CD8,CD14,CD16,CD19,CD20,CD25,CD36,CD56,TCRgd,GlyA,CD61,CD66b,CD123,HLA-DR,CD45RO\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = library protocol: 10x Gene Expression Flex\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample probe_barcode: CD4i_R1L11_D1_Rest : BC001+CR001|BC002+CR002|BC003+CR003|BC004+CR004, CD4i_R1L11_D1_Stim8hr : BC009+CR009|BC010+CR010|BC011+CR011|BC012+CR012, CD4i_R1L11_D2_Rest : BC005+CR005|BC006+CR006|BC007+CR007|BC008+CR008, CD4i_R1L11_D2_Stim8hr : BC013+CR013|BC014+CR014|BC015+CR015|BC016+CR016\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Naive human CD4+ T cells were isolated isolated with the EasySep Human Naive CD4+ T Cell Isolation Kit (catalog no. #19555, STEMCELL Technologies) according to the manufacturer’s protocol from PBMC-enriched leukapheresis products (Leukopaks, STEMCELL Technologies, catalog no. 70500) from healthy donors, after institutional review board–approved informed written consent (STEMCELL Technologies). After isolation (day 0), 30 million naive human CD4+ T cells were seeded at 1 x 106 cells/ml in X-VIVO 15 (Lonza Bioscience, catalog no. 04–418Q) supplemented with 5% fetal calf serum (FCS) (cXVIVO) and 200 IU/ml of recombinant human IL-2 (Amerisource Bergen, catalog no. 10101641). Cells were activated using ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator (10990, STEMCELL Technologies) at 25 µl/ml. The next morning, cells were transduced with 2% v/v concentrated ZIM3KRAB-dCas9-BlastR lentivirus. In the afternoon, cells were transduced with 0.1% v/v [multiplicity of infection (MOI) ~ 0.2] genome-scale sgRNA library lentivirus. At day 3, cells were centrifuged and resuspended with above medium supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2. Blasticidin and puromycin were added to 10 µg/mL and 2 µg/mL final concentrations, respectively. At day 5, cells were counted and diluted to 5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and 10 µg/mL blasticidin. Recombinant human IL-7 (R&D Systems, catalog no. 207-IL) was also added to a final concentration of 5 ng/mL. At day 7, cells were counted and diluted to 7.5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2, 5 ng/mL IL-7 and 10 µg/mL blasticidin. At both day 8 and day 10, cells were centrifuged and resuspended at 5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and 5 ng/mL IL-7. At day 12 morning, cells were centrifuged and resuspended at 1 x 106 cells/ml with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and split into three populations. The first population (Rest) was kept at a resting state without restimulation and harvested in the afternoon after 8 hours. The second population (Stim8hr) was restimulated by adding 12.5 µL/ml ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator and harvested in the afternoon after 8 hours. The third population (Stim48hr) was restimulated by adding 12.5 µL/ml ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator and harvested after 48 hours.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = GEM-X Flex Sample Preparation v2 Kit (10x genomics, catalog no. 1000781) per the manufacturer’s instructions\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: CD4i_R1L11_GEX_lib\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Raw data from pooled samples were processed by Cell Ranger v9.0.1 using the 2024-A probe set reference. UMI counts were demultiplexed back to each individual donor and stimulation condition using the barcodes in the sample_name: sample_probe_barcode metadata column.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = raw_matrix_genome_annotation:Chromium Human Transcriptome Probe Set v1.1.0: 2024-A , raw_matrix_value_units:UMI, raw_matrix_assays: scRNA-seq, CRISPR interference, raw_matrix_feature_keys:gene symbol for scRNA-seq, guide_id for CRISPR interference guides, raw_matrix_background_barcodes_included:False\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: h5, count matrix: scRNA-seq and crispr guide UMI\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL34762\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Lattice,,Data Coordination\r\n!Sample_contact_email = lattice-info@lists.stanford.edu\r\n!Sample_contact_department = Genetics\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Stanford University\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 3165 Porter Drive\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Palo Alto\r\n!Sample_contact_state = CA\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 94304\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = UG 100\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic single cell\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN53397159\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX31234203\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.ni