dded to a final concentration of 5 ng/mL. At day 7, cells were counted and diluted to 7.5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2, 5 ng/mL IL-7 and 10 µg/mL blasticidin. At both day 8 and day 10, cells were centrifuged and resuspended at 5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and 5 ng/mL IL-7. At day 12 morning, cells were centrifuged and resuspended at 1 x 106 cells/ml with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and split into three populations. The first population (Rest) was kept at a resting state without restimulation and harvested in the afternoon after 8 hours. The second population (Stim8hr) was restimulated by adding 12.5 µL/ml ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator and harvested in the afternoon after 8 hours. The third population (Stim48hr) was restimulated by adding 12.5 µL/ml ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator and harvested after 48 hours.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = GEM-X Flex Sample Preparation v2 Kit (10x genomics, catalog no. 1000781) per the manufacturer’s instructions\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: CD4i_R2L05_GEX_lib\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Raw data from pooled samples were processed by Cell Ranger v9.0.1 using the 2024-A probe set reference. UMI counts were demultiplexed back to each individual donor and stimulation condition using the barcodes in the sample_name: sample_probe_barcode metadata column.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = raw_matrix_genome_annotation:Chromium Human Transcriptome Probe Set v1.1.0: 2024-A , raw_matrix_value_units:UMI, raw_matrix_assays: scRNA-seq, CRISPR interference, raw_matrix_feature_keys:gene symbol for scRNA-seq, guide_id for CRISPR interference guides, raw_matrix_background_barcodes_included:False\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: h5, count matrix: scRNA-seq and crispr guide UMI\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL34762\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Lattice,,Data Coord