pended with above medium supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2. Blasticidin and puromycin were added to 10 µg/mL and 2 µg/mL final concentrations, respectively. At day 5, cells were counted and diluted to 5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and 10 µg/mL blasticidin. Recombinant human IL-7 (R&D Systems, catalog no. 207-IL) was also added to a final concentration of 5 ng/mL. At day 7, cells were counted and diluted to 7.5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2, 5 ng/mL IL-7 and 10 µg/mL blasticidin. At both day 8 and day 10, cells were centrifuged and resuspended at 5 x 105 cells/mL with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and 5 ng/mL IL-7. At day 12 morning, cells were centrifuged and resuspended at 1 x 106 cells/ml with cXVIVO supplemented with 200 IU/mL IL-2 and split into three populations. The first population (Rest) was kept at a resting state without restimulation and harvested in the afternoon after 8 hours. The second population (Stim8hr) was restimulated by adding 12.5 µL/ml ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator and harvested in the afternoon after 8 hours. The third population (Stim48hr) was restimulated by adding 12.5 µL/ml ImmunoCult human CD3/CD28/CD2 T cell activator and harvested after 48 hours.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = GEM-X Flex Sample Preparation v2 Kit (10x genomics, catalog no. 1000781) per the manufacturer’s instructions\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: CD4i_R2L10_GEX_lib\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Raw data from pooled samples were processed by Cell Ranger v9.0.1 using the 2024-A probe set reference. UMI counts were demultiplexed back to each individual donor and stimulation condition using the barcodes in the sample_name: sample_probe_barcode metadata column.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = raw_matrix_genome_annotation:Chromium Human Transcriptome Probe Set v1.1.0: 2024-A , raw_matrix_value_units:UMI, raw_matrix_assays: scRNA-seq, CRISPR interference, raw_matrix_feature_keys:gene symbol for scRNA-seq, guide_id for CRISPR interference guides, raw_matrix_background_barcodes_included:False\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: h5, count matrix: scRNA-seq and crispr guide UMI\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL34762\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Lattice,,Data Coordination\r\n!Sample_contact_email = lattice-info@lists.stanford.edu\r\n!Sample_contact_department = Genetics\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Stanford University\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 3165 Porter Drive\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Palo Alto\r\n!Sample_contact_state = CA\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 94304\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = UG 100\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic single cell\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN53795499\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX31394615\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9393nnn/GSM9393860/suppl/GSM9393860_CD4i_R2L10_D3_Rest_sample_filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_2 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9393nnn/GSM9393860/suppl/GSM9393860_CD4i_R2L10_D3_Stim8hr_sample_filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_3 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9393nnn/GSM9393860/suppl/GSM9393860_CD4i_R2L10_D4_Rest_sample_filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_4 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9393nnn/GSM9393860/suppl/GSM9393860_CD4i_R2L10_D4_Stim8hr_sample_filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE314342\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM9393861\r\n!Sample_title = CD4i_R2L11_GEX:scRNA-seq CRISPR interference screen of CD4+, ⍺β T cells, 2 pooled donors, resting and 8 hr stim\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9393861\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Feb 0