1.1.0. Alignment quality metrics, strand specificity, and read distribution across genomic features were assessed using RSeQC v5.0.4 and Qualimap v2.3, with results aggregated into a comprehensive quality control report using MultiQC v1.32. Gene-level expression quantification was performed using featureCounts (subread package v2.1.1) with strand-specific counting, multi-mapping read fractional assignment, exons and three prime UTR as the feature identifiers, and grouped by gene_id. Final gene counts were annotated with gene biotype and other metadata extracted from the reference GTF file.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38, GENCODE48\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: processed data format:csv, processed data content: raw counts, normalized counts (CPM)\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL34284\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Lattice,,Data Coordination\r\n!Sample_contact_email = lattice-info@lists.stanford.edu\r\n!Sample_contact_department = Genetics\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Stanford University\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 3165 Porter Drive\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Palo Alto\r\n!Sample_contact_state = CA\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 94304\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq X Plus\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN54878393\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX31930742\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE314342\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM9481733\r\n!Sample_title = Donor 9 cells perturbed with SGF29 knockdown by CRISPRi\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9481733\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Feb 06 2026\r\n!Sample_submission_date = Jan 28 2026\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Feb 06 2026\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_sour