characteristics_ch1 = cell type: T cell\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = We chose the Jurkat E6 cell line expressing dCas9-KRAB as our model to study. We transduced them with a genome-wide CRISPRi CROP-seq library at a high multiplicity of infection (MOI). The FACS-measured percentage of GFP positive cells was 99.6%, translating to an estimated MOI of ~6. From experience, we know that real MOI is typically higher than what is estimated from GFP positivity rate. After infection, we split the cells into two populations, including untreated cells and activated cells (cells treated with anti-TCR and anti-CD28 antibodies for approximately 24 hours to stimulate TCR signaling). Cells were then labelled with cell hashing antibodies. Multiple labels were used for the activated population to help with cell multiplet detection. Cells were loaded on 16 channels of 10x Chromium X instrument. We loaded on 115,000 cells per channel and the expected recovery rate was 60,000 cells per channel, including 24% multiplets. Samples were pooled unequally before they were loaded on the Chromium X: 10% untreated cells, 90% treated cells. A sequencing library was prepared using 3’Chemistry with a targeted primer panel: custom multiplex PCR step to enrich for specific transcript. Libraries were sequenced on NovaSeq S4 PE100 in asymetric read mode (R1: 28 cycles; R2: 172 cycles), with PhiX concentration of 1%. The expected coverage is around 9,000 to 10,000 input reads per cell.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The genome-wide CRISPRi sgRNA library was designed to target the transcription start site (TSS) coordinates, calculated from publicly available FANTOM CAGE peaks data. In total 18,595 genes were targeted, with 4 sgRNAs per gene. Additionally, we designed another CRISPRi library targeting 3,220 genes with 4 sgRNAs per gene. This library was designed using TSS data specific to Jurkat cells, calculated from publicly accessible Jurkat CAGE-seq datasets. Both libraries were combined into a final library targeting 3,220 genes with 8 sgRNAs per gene and 15,375 genes with 4 sgRNAs per gene.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = For each of the 16 channels, all three types of sequencing libraries (mRNA, sgRNA, cell hashing) were uniquely indexed with the same Illumina index sequence. This results in a single pair of fastq files for each channel, necessitating computational separation of the three library types. Transcriptomic reads were mapped using STAR and STARsolo 2.7.10a against a custom gtf annotation based on gencode.v34.annotation.gtf (hg38). Reads that did not map to the transcriptome reference were subsequently mapped and counted using STARsolo against a custom fasta reference containing guide sequences and a fasta reference with hash label sequences.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = The output transcriptome matrices from STARsolo underwent initial filtering, akin to the 10x Cell Ranger EmptyDrops filtering method. This retained cells with at least 10% UMI count of the 99th percentile UMI counts of the top expected cells number. From these filtered matrices, an initial Seurat object was created using CreateSeuratObject function with parameters min.cells = 5, min.features = 10, and all other parameters at default values. Mitochondrial and mRNA content (percent.mt, nCount_RNA) were used to filter out outlier cells. To identify cell multiplets and determine cell population (untreated or activated), cell labels (hashes) were called using MULTI-seq approach (deMULTIplex::classifyCells in R). Only cells with exactly one known label were retained. Then, sgRNA calling was performed using a binomial test, with total sgRNA UMI counts used to derive background frequencies. A threshold of 0.05 on Benjamini-Hochberg- corrected p-values (per channel) was used to generate the final calls.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = The sgRNA assays produced sparse matrices where a value of 1 indicates that the respective cell is carrying the corresponding sgRNA, and 0 elsewhere. Following these steps, results from 16 channels were merged together, and the merged counts were normalized using NormalizeData and scaled using ScaleData. Cell cycle scoring was performed via CellCycleScoring , PCA was calculated using RunPCA, and UMAP was calculated on first 30 principal components using RunUMAP in Seurat.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Tab-separated values files and matrix files\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: Perturb-seq\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Bicna,,Song\r\n!Sample_contact_email = bsong@childrensnational.org\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Children's National Hospital\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 7144 13th Pl NW\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Washington\r\n!Sample_contact_state = DC\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 20012\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000\r\n!Sample_library_selection = other\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN38711292\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX22812240\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM7951nnn/GSM7951418/suppl/GSM7951418_channel6_guides_barcode.tsv.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_2 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM7951nnn/GSM7951418/suppl/GSM7951418_channel6_guides_features.tsv.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_3 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM7951nnn/GSM7951418/suppl/GSM7951418_channel6_guides_matrix.mtx.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_4 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM7951nnn/GSM7951418/suppl/GSM7951418_channel6_labels_barcode.tsv.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_5 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM7951nnn/GSM7951418/suppl/GSM7951418_channel6_labels_features.tsv.gz\r\n!Samp