-017-1382-0\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Virshup I, Bredikhin D, Heumos L, Palla G, Sturm G, Gayoso A, et al. The scverse project provides a computational ecosystem for single-cell omics data analysis. Nat Biotechnol. 2023;41: 604–606. doi:10.1038/s41587-023-01733-8\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Love MI, Huber W, Anders S. Moderated estimation of fold change and dispersion for RNA-seq data with DESeq2. Genome Biol. 2014;15: 550. doi:10.1186/s13059-014-0550-8\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Heumos L, Ji Y, May L, Green T, Zhang X, Wu X, et al. Pertpy: an end-to-end framework for perturbation analysis. bioRxiv. 2024. doi:10.1101/2024.08.04.606516\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Muzellec B, Teleńczuk M, Cabeli V, Andreux M. PyDESeq2: a python package for bulk RNA-seq differential expression analysis. Bioinformatics. 2023;39: btad547. doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btad547\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Peidli S, Green TD, Shen C, Gross T, Min J, Garda S, et al. scPerturb: harmonized single-cell perturbation data. Nat Methods. 2024;21: 531–540. doi:10.1038/s41592-023-02144-y\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Urbut SM, Wang G, Carbonetto P, Stephens M. Flexible statistical methods for estimating and testing effects in genomic studies with multiple conditions. Nat Genet. 2019;51: 187–195. doi:10.1038/s41588-018-0268-8\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Karlsson M, Zhang C, Méar L, Zhong W, Digre A, Katona B, et al. A single-cell type transcriptomics map of human tissues. Sci Adv. 2021;7: eabh2169. doi:10.1126/sciadv.abh2169\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Uhlén M, Fagerberg L, Hallström BM, Lindskog C, Oksvold P, Mardinoglu A, et al. Proteomics. Tissue-based map of the human proteome. Science. 2015;347: 1260419. doi:10.1126/science.1260419\" />\n<meta name=\"citation_reference\" content=\"Yanai I, Benjamin H, Shmoish M, Chalifa-Caspi