  "content_type": "geo/text",
  "text": "^SAMPLE = GSM6858447\r\n!Sample_title = THP-1 cells, conventional KO screen\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM6858447\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jan 01 2023\r\n!Sample_submission_date = Dec 19 2022\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jul 13 2023\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Cas9-expressing THP-1\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: Cas9-expressing THP-1\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Macrophage\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: 3 hours LPS\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = THP-1 cell lines were infected with sgRNA libraries at a multiplicity of infection (MOI) specific for each experiment. 12 hours after spinfection, cells and media were diluted 1:10 and cells were allowed to recover for 48h. Cells were selected with puromycin (2 micrograms/mL) for four days. The selected cells were differentiated into macrophages by stimulation in 20ng/mL phorbol 12-myristate 13-acetate (Sigma Aldrich, P8139-1mg) for 24 hours. Cells were then allowed to rest in normal culture medium for 48 hours before stimulation in medium containing 100ng/mL LPS (Millipore sigma, L4391-1mg) for 3 hours.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = THP-1 cells (ATCC, TIB202) were cultured in RPMI medium (ATCC, 30-2001) supplemented with 10% FBS (ATCC, 30-2020) and 0.05mM 2-mercaptoethanol (sigma Aldrich, M7522). Cells were maintained between 0.8 and 2 million cells per milliliter.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The THP-1 cell suspension was prepared for droplet generation according to the manufacturer’s suggested protocol (10x Genomics, CG00053 Rev C).\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The standard 10x single cell 3’ RNAseq protocol (Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 3’ GEM, Library & Gel Bead Kit v3.1 PN-1000121) was run according to manufacturer's recommendation.\r\n!Sample_description = 10X Genomics\r\n!Sample_data_processing = The “cellranger mkfastq” command with default parameters (from the 10x CellRanger tool v6.0.1; https://support.10xgenomics.com/single-cell-gene-expression/software/downloads/latest) was used to generate FASTQ files.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = The “cellranger count” command with default parameters was used to align the expression reads to the GRCh38 build of the human transcriptome and generate a gene expression count matrix.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: All expression counts stored as Seurat object (R data set file format). Expression counts are stored under the \"RNA\" assay, while cell by perturbation design matrix stored under the \"perturbations\" assay. Cell meta-data is stored in the Seurat metadata.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: All expression counts stored as Anndata object (h5ad file format). Object contains expression counts and cell meta-data but not perturbation by cell design matrix.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Perturbation by cell design matrix (tab-delimited text file). Rows correspond to perturbations and columns correspond to cells. Entries of the matrix indicate how many unique guides the cell contains for the given perturbation (ranging from 0 to 4).\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: KO_all_FRPerturb_effect_sizes.csv: Log fold changes and qvalues of all perturbation-on-gene effects estimated by FR-Perturb (conventional and pooled samples combined when inferring effects).\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: KO_conventional_FRPerturb_effect_sizes.csv: Log fold changes and qvalues of all perturbation-on-gene effects estimated by FR-Perturb.\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL20795\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Douglas,,Yao\r\n!Sample_contact_email = douglasyao@g.harvard.edu\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Harvard University\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 1350 Massachusetts Ave\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Cambridge\r\n!Sample_contact_state = MA\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 02138\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = HiSeq X Ten\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic single cell\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN32312808\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX18774274\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM6858nnn/GSM6858447/suppl/GSM6858447_KO_all_FRPerturb_effect_sizes.csv.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_2 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM6858nnn/GSM6858447/suppl/GSM6858447_KO_conventional.h5ad.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_3 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM6858nnn/GSM6858447/suppl/GSM6858447_KO_conventional.rds.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_4 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM6858nnn/GSM6858447/suppl/GSM6858447_KO_conventional_FRPerturb_effect_sizes.csv.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_5 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM6858nnn/GSM6858447/suppl/GSM6858447_KO_conventional_perturbations.txt.gz\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE221321\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM6858448\r\n!Sample_title = THP-1 cells, cell-pooled KO screen\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM6858448\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jan 01 2023\r\n!Sample_submission_date = Dec 19 2022\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jul 13 2023\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Cas9-expressing THP-1\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: Cas9-expressing THP-1\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Macrophage\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: 3 hours LPS\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = THP-1 cell lines were infected with sgRNA libraries at a m