  "text": "^SAMPLE = GSM8252546\r\n!Sample_title = CD4, 0h, SafeHarbor, CART0077_D1\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8252546\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jul 22 2025\r\n!Sample_submission_date = May 05 2024\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jul 22 2025\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = CD4\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: CD4\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: SafeHarbor\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment hours: 0\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor: CART0077_D1\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = Sex: Female\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = CAR T cells were repeatedly stimulated with irradiated CD19+ K562 tumor cells at 1:1 ratio and sampled at day 0, 3, 7 and 10.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Human primary T cells were isolated from the whole blood of three independent healthy donors. Cells were stimulated with anti-CD3/CD28 reagent. After 2 days, cells were transduced with CROP-seq-CAR lentivirus to deliver the CAR and a library of 8 gRNAs targeting either RHOG or a safe harbor locus. Puromycin was added 2 days later to select for the lentiviral construct. After a total of 7 days from initial stimulation, cells were restimulated with anti-CD3/CD28 reagent. After 2 days, cells were electroporated with synthetic mRNA for Cas9 and blasticidin resistance. Blasticidin was added 24 hours later and kept for 2 days in the culture medium to select for successful electroporation. 6 days later, CRISPR-modified CAR T cells were used for the RNA-seq readout.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = To isolate pure CD4 or CD8 cells from primary T cell culture and co-culture with irradiated tumor cells, we used the EasySep Human CD4 Positive Selection Kit II (Stemcell #17852) and EasySep Human CD8 Positive Selection Kit II (Stemcell #17853). RNA was isolated using the Monarch Total RNA Miniprep Kit (NEB #T2010S) from at least 200,000 lysed cells and stored at -80 ˚C in 300 µl of Protection Reagent.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Sequencing libraries were prepared with the NEBNext Ultra II Directional RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (NEB #E7760L).\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA-seq libraries were sequenced by the Biomedical Sequencing Facility at the CeMM Research Center for Molecular Medicine of the Austrian Academy of Sciences, on the Illumina NovaSeq 6000 platform and the 50 bp paired-end configuration.\r\n!Sample_description = CART0077_RNAseq_NgsRun1_001\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Alignment using STAR\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Count matrix aggregated using the wrapper from\r\n!Sample_data_processing = snakemake-workflows/rna-seq-star-deseq2\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Comma-separated file includes aggregated counts for each sample\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Christoph,,Bock\r\n!Sample_contact_email = cbock@cemm.oeaw.ac.at\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = CeMM Research Center for Molecular Medicine of the Austrian Academy of Sciences\r\n!Sample_contact_address = Lazarettgasse 14\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Vienna\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 1090\r\n!Sample_contact_country = Austria\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE266618\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM8252547\r\n!Sample_title = CD4, 0h, RHOG, CART0077_D1\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8252547\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jul 22 2025\r\n!Sample_submission_date = May 05 2024\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jul 22 2025\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = CD4\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: CD4\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: RHOG\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment hours: 0\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = donor: CART0077_D1\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = Sex: Female\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = CAR T cells were repeatedly stimulated with irradiated CD19+ K562 tumor cells at 1:1 ratio and sampled at day 0, 3, 7 and 10.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Human primary T cells were isolated from the whole blood of three independent healthy donors. Cells were stimulated with anti-CD3/CD28 reagent. After 2 days, cells were transduced with CROP-seq-CAR lentivirus to deliver the CAR and a library of 8 gRNAs targeting either RHOG or a safe harbor locus. Puromycin was added 2 days later to select for the lentiviral construct. After a total of 7 days from initial stimulation, cells were restimulated with anti-CD3/CD28 reagent. After 2 days, cells were electroporated with synthetic mRNA for Cas9 and blasticidin resistance. Blasticidin was added 24 hours later and kept for 2 days in the culture medium to select for successful electroporation. 6 days later, CRISPR-modified CAR T cells were used for the RNA-seq readout.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = To isolate pure CD4 or CD8 cells from primary T cell culture and co-culture with irradiated tumor cells, we used the EasySep Human CD4 Positive Selection Kit II (Stemcell #17852) and EasySep Human CD8 Positive Selection Kit II (Stemcell #17853). RNA was isolated using the Monarch Total RNA Miniprep Kit (NEB #T2010S) from at least 200,000 lysed cells and stored at -80 ˚C in 300 µl of Protection Reagent.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Sequencing libraries were prepared with the NEBNext Ultra II Directional RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (NEB #E7760L).\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA-seq libraries were sequenced by the Biomedical Sequencing Facility at the CeMM Research Center for Molecular Medicine of the Austri