eting financial interests.</p><p id=\"P46\">Reprints and permissions information is available online at <ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"http://www.nature.com/reprints/index.html\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">http://www.nature.com/reprints/index.html</ext-link>.</p></fn><fn id=\"FN3\"><p id=\"P47\"><bold>Reagent and data availability</bold></p><p id=\"P48\">The CROPseq-Guide-Puro plasmid is available from Addgene (86708). Raw and processed CROP- seq data are provided via the NCBI GEO database (<ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE92872\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">GSE92872</ext-link>). The source code of the computational analyses is included as <xref rid=\"SD4\" ref-type=\"supplementary-material\">Supplementary Software</xref> and maintained in an open Github repository (<ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"https://github.com/epigen/crop-seq\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">https://github.com/epigen/crop-seq</ext-link>).</p></fn><fn id=\"FN4\"><p id=\"P49\"><bold>Accession codes</bold></p><p id=\"P50\">Raw and processed CROP-seq data are available from NCBI GEO under accession number <ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE92872\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">GSE92872</ext-link>.</p></fn></fn-group></sec><sec id=\"ref-list1\" sec-type=\"ref-list\" disp-level=\"1\"><title>References</title><sec id=\"ref-list1_sec2\" disp-level=\"2\"><ref-list><ref id=\"R1\"><label>1.</label><mixed-citation><named-content content-type=\"citation-string\">Blomen VA, et al.  Gene essentiality and synthetic lethality in haploid human cells. Science. 2015;350:1092–1096. doi: 10.1126/science.aac7557.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" ext-link-type=\"doi\" xlink:href=\"10.1126/science.aac7557\"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" ex