  "content_type": "geo/text",
  "text": "^SAMPLE = GSM9070957\r\n!Sample_title = MSC-NC-rep1\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9070957\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jun 27 2025\r\n!Sample_submission_date = Jun 26 2025\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 27 2025\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Human MSCs were first transduced with a lentiviral construct expressing dCas9-KRAB (e.g., pSLQ6604 driven by the SFFV promoter) and cultured for 3 days to allow protein expression. Cells were then sorted based on KRAB expression to enrich for successfully transduced populations. These enriched cells were subsequently transduced with individual lentiviral sgRNAs and cultured for 72 hours, followed by puromycin selection (2 μg/mL) for 48 hours to ensure sgRNA integration. After selection, cells were allowed to recover and expand over several passages. Finally, RNA was harvested for downstream transcriptional profiling. Where indicated, cells were treated with 10 ng/mL recombinant human IL-6 (Abcam, ab259381) to assess inflammatory senescence phenotypes under cytokine-induced stress.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Primary adipose derived cell (Lifeline) were maintained on gelatin-coated tissue culture plates with medium specific for MSC growing (StemLife MSC Medium Complete Kit, Lifeline) .Cells were maintained at 37℃ in a cell incubator containing 5% CO2.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = As indicated, cells were harvested and RNA was extracted from all samples\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA quantity and integrity were assessed using an Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer. Only samples with RNA integrity number (RIN) ≥8 were used for downstream processing. For library preparation, 500 ng to 1 µg of high-quality total RNA was used as input. mRNA was enriched using poly(A) selection with oligo-dT magnetic beads to isolate polyadenylated transcripts. Strand-specific RNA-seq libraries were constructed using the NEBNext Ultra II Directional RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (New England Biolabs), following the manufacturer’s protocol. Libraries were indexed, PCR-amplified, purified, and size-selected (~300 bp inserts), and quality control was performed using Qubit and Bioanalyzer prior to sequencing.\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: M1_1\r\n!Sample_data_processing = STAR 2.7.11b was used to align paired reads to the genome index. Command: STAR --runThreadN 8 --genomeDir {dirname_here} --readFilesIn '{fname_here} {fname_here} --readFilesCommand zcat --outFileNamePrefix --outFileNamePrefix {user_option} --outSAMattributes Standard --outSAMstrandField intronMotif --outSAMtype BAM SortedByCoordinate Htseq-count was used to calculate read counts. Command: htseq-count -i gene_id {bam_fname_here} {gtf_fname_here} -r pos -s no -f bam > {output_fname_here} Fragments per kilobase transcript per million mapped reads (FPKM) were quantified by the following method: for each sample, for each gene HTseq-count values were divided by gene length in kilobases (quantified by GTFtools; Command: python2.7 GTFtools_0.6.9/gtftools.py -l {output_fname} {gtf_fname}) and divided the total sample count in millions.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Read counts calculated by Htseq at different conditions (ISS, RSS, with and without IL-6) for two biological replicates.\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL34284\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Betty Chentzu,,Yu\r\n!Sample_contact_email = cyu3@fredhutch.org\r\n!Sample_contact_department = Computational Biology\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 1100 Fairview Ave N\r\n!Sam