atin-coated tissue culture plates with medium specific for MSC growing (StemLife MSC Medium Complete Kit, Lifeline) .Cells were maintained at 37℃ in a cell incubator containing 5% CO2.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = As indicated, cells were harvested and RNA was extracted from all samples\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA quantity and integrity were assessed using an Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer. Only samples with RNA integrity number (RIN) ≥8 were used for downstream processing. For library preparation, 500 ng to 1 µg of high-quality total RNA was used as input. mRNA was enriched using poly(A) selection with oligo-dT magnetic beads to isolate polyadenylated transcripts. Strand-specific RNA-seq libraries were constructed using the NEBNext Ultra II Directional RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (New England Biolabs), following the manufacturer’s protocol. Libraries were indexed, PCR-amplified, purified, and size-selected (~300 bp inserts), and quality control was performed using Qubit and Bioanalyzer prior to sequencing.\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: IP2_2\r\n!Sample_data_processing = STAR 2.7.11b was used to align paired reads to the genome index. Command: STAR --runThreadN 8 --genomeDir {dirname_here} --readFilesIn '{fname_here} {fname_here} --readFilesCommand zcat --outFileNamePrefix --outFileNamePrefix {user_option} --outSAMattributes Standard --outSAMstrandField intronMotif --outSAMtype BAM SortedByCoordinate Htseq-count was used to calculate read counts. Command: htseq-count -i gene_id {bam_fname_here} {gtf_fname_here} -r pos -s no -f bam > {output_fname_here} Fragments per kilobase transcript per million mapped reads (FPKM) were quantified by the following method: for each sample, for each gene HTseq-count values were divided by gene length in kilobases (quantified by GTFtools; Command: python2.7 GTFtools_0.6.9/gtftools.py -l {output_fname} {gtf_fname}) and divided the total sample count in millions.\r\n!Sample_da