  "text": "^SAMPLE = GSM8294345\r\n!Sample_title = d0_rep1\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8294345\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jun 20 2025\r\n!Sample_submission_date = May 29 2024\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 20 2025\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: mesenchymal stem cells\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: --\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = The senescence screens were performed in two independent replicates. 1. On day −3, 125M MSC cells were seeded at 2.5M cells/15cm gelatin-coated dishes; 2. On day −1, cells were transduced with pooled lentiviral sgRNA library with a MOI of 0.3; 3. On day 0, cells were switched to basal medium with and puromycin at 2μg/mL; 4. 7days after puromycin selection, 25 million cells were harvested as the initial population of the screen. 5. Fresh medium with puromycin at 1μg/mL was changed every day starting day 7; 6. On day 14，cells intergrated lentiviral sgRNA libray were transduced with a lentiviral constructs pSLQ6604 that express dCas9-KRAB from SFFVpromoter 7. On day 17, cells were harvested and divided into 2 parts: one part is for growing naturally until their growing limitation, other part is for growing in the presence of 10ng/ml recombinant human IL-6 protein(Abcam, ab259381) until their growing limitation. Fresh medium was changed every 2 days.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Primary adipose derived cell (Lifeline) were maintained on gelatin-coated tissue culture plates with medium specific for MSC growing (StemLife MSC Medium Complete Kit, Lifeline) .Human embryonic kidney (HEK293T) cells (ATCC) were cultured in 10% fetal bovine serum (Thermo Fisher Scientific) in DMEM (Thermo Fisher Scientific). Cells were maintained at 37℃ in a cell incubator containing 5% CO2.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = About 7-8weeks later, cells were harvested and genomic DNA was extracted from all samples\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The sgRNA-encoding regions were then amplified by PCR using HiSeq forward and reverse primers and then sequenced on an Illumina HiSeq-4000 using HiSeq custom primer with previously described protocols at high coverage. Primers used are summarized in TableS3.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = We calculated the gRNA count matrix by exact match for each read. Counts between replicates of the same condition were highly correlated (Pearson correlation coefficient was 0.835 for the RSS day 30 sample, and 0.894 for the ISS D30 screening sample), indicating the high reproducibility of the RSS and ISS CRISPRi screening.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = The gRNA count table was loaded into MaGeCK (Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout) to use the maximum likelihood estimation (MLE) approach to estimate the essentiality of genes in cell senescence by comparing the experimental in replicative arrest and inflammation (IL6 stimulation) condition. The beta score was calculated to call gene essentialities: a positive beta score means a gene is positively selected (the gene expression positively functions in cell senescence), and a negative beta score means a gene is negatively selected (the gene expression negatively functions in cell senescence).\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg19\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: CountMatrix.xlsx file: sequenced  sgRNA counts mapped to the sgRNA library at different conditions (d0, without and with  IL-6)  for two biological replicates\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR screen\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL20301\r\n!Sample_contact_name = xueqiu,,lin\r\n!Sample_contact_email = xueqiu@fredhutch.org\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = FRED HUTCHINSON CANCER CENTER\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 1100 Fairview Ave N\r\n!Sample_contact_city = seattle\r\n!Sample_contact_state = wa\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 98109\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 4000\r\n!Sample_library_selection = other\r\n!Sample_library_source = genomic\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN41581376\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX24738045\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE268569\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM8294346\r\n!Sample_title = d0_rep2\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8294346\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jun 20 2025\r\n!Sample_submission_date = May 29 2024\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 20 2025\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: mesenchymal stem cells\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: --\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = The senescence screens were performed in two independent replicates. 1. On day −3, 125M MSC cells were seeded at 2.5M cells/15cm gelatin-coated dishes; 2. On day −1, cells were transduced with pooled lentiviral sgRNA library with a MOI of 0.3; 3. On day 0, cells were switched to basal medium with and puromycin at 2μg/mL; 4. 7days after puromycin selection, 25 million cells were harvested as the initial population of the screen. 5. Fresh medium with puromycin at 1μg/mL was changed every day starting day 7; 6. On day 14，cells intergrated lentiviral sgRNA libray were transduced with a lentiviral constructs pSLQ6604 that express dCas9-KRAB from SFFVpromoter 7. On day 17, cells were harvested and divided into 2 parts: one part is for growing naturally until their growing limitation, other part is for growing in the presence of 10ng/ml recombinant human IL-6 protein(Abcam, ab259381) until their growing limitation. Fresh medium was changed every 2 days.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Primary adipose derived cell (Lifeline) were maintained on gelatin-coated tissue culture plates with medium specific for MSC growing (StemLife MSC Medium Complete Kit, Lifeline) .Human embryonic kidney (HEK293T) cells (ATCC) were cultured in 10% fetal bovine serum (Thermo Fisher Scientific) in DMEM (Thermo Fisher Scientific). Cells were maintained at 37℃ in a cell incubator containing 5% CO2.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = About 7-8weeks later, cells were harvested and genomic DNA was extracted from all samples\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The sgRNA-encoding regions were then amplified by PCR using HiSeq forward and reverse primers and then sequenced on an Illumina HiSeq-4000 using HiSeq custom primer with previously described protocols at high coverage. Primers used are summarized in TableS3.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = We calculated the gRNA count matrix by exact match for each read. Counts between replicates of the same condition were highly correlated (Pearson correlation coefficient was 0.835 for the RSS day 30 sample, and 0.894 for the ISS D30 screening sample), indicating the high reproducibility of the RSS and ISS CRISPRi screening.\r\n!Sample_data_processing = The gRNA count table was loaded into MaGeCK (Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout) to use the maximum likelihood estimation (MLE) approach to estimate the essentiality of genes in cell senescence by comparing the experimental in replicative arrest and inflammation (IL6 stimulation) condition. The beta score was calculated to call gene essentialities: a positive beta score means a gene is positively selected (the gene expression positively functions in cell senescence), and a negative beta score means a gene is negatively selected (the gene expression negatively functions in cell senescence).\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg19\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: CountMatrix.xlsx file: sequenced  sgRNA counts mapped to the sgRNA library at different conditions (d0, without and with  IL-6)  for two biological replicates\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR screen\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL20301\r\n!Sample_contact_name = xueqiu,,lin\r\n!Sample_contact_email = xueqiu@fredhutch.org\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = FRED HUTCHINSON CANCER CENTER\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 1100 Fairview Ave N\r\n!Sample_contact_city = seattle\r\n!Sample_contact_state = wa\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 98109\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 4000\r\n!Sample_library_selection = other\r\n!Sample_library_source = genomic\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN41581375\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX24738046\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE268569\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM8294347\r\n!Sample_title = Il6m_rep1\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8294347\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jun 20 2025\r\n!Sample_submission_date = May 29 2024\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 20 2025\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: human primary mesenchymal stem cells (MSC) derived from adipose tissues\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: mesenchymal stem cells\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = trea