  "text": "^SAMPLE = GSM9268463\r\n!Sample_title = CRISPRa screen and dial-up scRNA-seq, WI-38 fibroblasts, array1\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9268463\r\n!Sample_status = Public on Jun 23 2026\r\n!Sample_submission_date = Sep 29 2025\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 23 2026\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = WI-38\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: WI-38\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: fibroblast\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Dial-up transcript enrichment from single-cell WTA libraries was performed using a two-step PCR strategy. Target-specific primers for p16, p15, p14, and ANRIL were combined with a CA-SMART reverse primer to selectively amplify transcripts of interest while retaining cell barcodes and UMIs from the Seq-Well protocol. Amplified products underwent bead cleanup, followed by biotin pull-down (Dynabeads™ kilobaseBINDER™ Kit, Thermo 60101) to enrich the targeted transcripts, which were then eluted for downstream processing. See Methods section of the paper for further details.  WI-38 fibroblasts (ATCC CCL-75) were transduced with pooled CRISPRa libraries (771 gRNAs targeting 175 regions plus 83 controls; designed by the Broad Genetic Perturbation Platform) using a three-vector system (CROP-sgRNA-MS2, lenti dCAS-VP64_Blast, lentiMPH v2). Viral transductions were performed in HEK293FT cells and applied to WI-38 cells with polybrene. After 4–8 days, cells were harvested for single-cell RNA-seq.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Dial-up transcripts were subjected to a second PCR to add Illumina sequencing adapters (P5, P7), dual indices (i5, i7), and sequencing primer binding sites. Amplified libraries were purified with a 0.9X bead cleanup and eluted in 1X TE. Final libraries were sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 using a 75-cycle kit with custom read 1 and custom i5 primers (20 cycles read 1 for cell barcode + UMI, 56 cycles read 2 for transcript sequence, and 2 × 8-bp index reads). See Methods section of the paper.  Single-cell RNA-seq was performed using Seq-Well (Gierahn et al. 2017; Aicher et al. 2019). Cells were loaded onto microwell arrays preloaded with poly-T capture beads, sealed with a semipermeable membrane, lysed, and mRNAs hybridized to beads. Reverse transcription, second-strand synthesis, and whole-transcriptome amplification were performed on-bead. Libraries were prepared via tagmentation (Illumina) and sequenced on an Illumina platform. for further details\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: array1_dial-up_CROP\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Demultiplexed fastqs were aligned with STAR solo\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Raw STAR solo outputs: barcodes.tsv.gz, features.tsv.gz, matrix.mtx.gz\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR Screen\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Neva,Cherniavsky,Durand\r\n!Sample_contact_email = neva@broadinstitute.org\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Broad Institute\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 75 Ames St\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Cambridge\r\n!Sample_contact_state = MA\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 02139\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 500\r\n!Sample_library_selection = other\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN52065059\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX30720981\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9268nnn/GSM9268463/suppl/GSM9268463_new-screen-CROP-orig-stitch-array1_barcodes.tsv.gz\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_2 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9268nnn/GSM9268463/suppl/GSM9268463_new-screen-CROP-orig-stitch-array1_features.tsv.gz