), and sequencing primer binding sites. Amplified libraries were purified with a 0.9X bead cleanup and eluted in 1X TE. Final libraries were sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 using a 75-cycle kit with custom read 1 and custom i5 primers (20 cycles read 1 for cell barcode + UMI, 56 cycles read 2 for transcript sequence, and 2 × 8-bp index reads). See Methods section of the paper.  Single-cell RNA-seq was performed using Seq-Well (Gierahn et al. 2017; Aicher et al. 2019). Cells were loaded onto microwell arrays preloaded with poly-T capture beads, sealed with a semipermeable membrane, lysed, and mRNAs hybridized to beads. Reverse transcription, second-strand synthesis, and whole-transcriptome amplification were performed on-bead. Libraries were prepared via tagmentation (Illumina) and sequenced on an Illumina platform. for further details\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: array1_mRNA\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Demultiplexed fastqs were aligned with STAR solo\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Raw STAR solo outputs: barcodes.tsv.gz, features.tsv.gz, matrix.mtx.gz\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Neva,Cherniavsky,Durand\r\n!Sample_contact_email = neva@broadinstitute.org\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Broad Institute\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 75 Ames St\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Cambridge\r\n!Sample_contact_state = MA\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 02139\r\n!Sample_contact_country = USA\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 500\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic single cell\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN52065058\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX30720982\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9268nnn/GSM9268464/suppl/GSM9268464_mRNA_array1_barcodes.tsv.g