3 controls; designed by the Broad Genetic Perturbation Platform) using a three-vector system (CROP-sgRNA-MS2, lenti dCAS-VP64_Blast, lentiMPH v2). Viral transductions were performed in HEK293FT cells and applied to WI-38 cells with polybrene. After 4–8 days, cells were harvested for single-cell RNA-seq.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Dial-up transcripts were subjected to a second PCR to add Illumina sequencing adapters (P5, P7), dual indices (i5, i7), and sequencing primer binding sites. Amplified libraries were purified with a 0.9X bead cleanup and eluted in 1X TE. Final libraries were sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 using a 75-cycle kit with custom read 1 and custom i5 primers (20 cycles read 1 for cell barcode + UMI, 56 cycles read 2 for transcript sequence, and 2 × 8-bp index reads). See Methods section of the paper.  Single-cell RNA-seq was performed using Seq-Well (Gierahn et al. 2017; Aicher et al. 2019). Cells were loaded onto microwell arrays preloaded with poly-T capture beads, sealed with a semipermeable membrane, lysed, and mRNAs hybridized to beads. Reverse transcription, second-strand synthesis, and whole-transcriptome amplification were performed on-bead. Libraries were prepared via tagmentation (Illumina) and sequenced on an Illumina platform. for further details\r\n!Sample_description = Library name: array15_dial-up_CROP\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Demultiplexed fastqs were aligned with STAR solo\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Raw STAR solo outputs: barcodes.tsv.gz, features.tsv.gz, matrix.mtx.gz\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR Screen\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Neva,Cherniavsky,Durand\r\n!Sample_contact_email = neva@broadinstitute.org\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = Broad Institute\r\n!Sample_contact_address = 75 Ames St\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Cambridge\r\n!Sample_contact_state = MA\r\n!Sample_contact_zi