 Premium (LBPX1500, OZBiosciences, which also enhances hematopoietic cell transduction), and the media was replenished the next day with BM media supplemented with cytokines.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = The primary AML samples/PDX samples were obtained from the Stem Cell and Xenograft Core Facility at The Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania or xxx, after informed consent in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki. Protocols used for this study were approved by the University Pennsylvania’s institutional review board. The primary AML samples were frozen in FCS and 10% DMSO in liquid nitrogen for long-term storage. Patient clinical info is included in Table Sx. For short-term in vitro maintenance, cells were cultured in BM media (IMDM supplemented with 15% Fetal Bovine Serum (FBS), 1% P/S, 1% GlutaMAX) supplemented with human cytokines including 10ng/μl human IL-3 (200-03), 10ng/μl human FLT3 (300-19), 100ng/μl humanSCF (300-07), 20ng/μl humanIL-6 (200-06) and 10 ng/μl humanTPO (300-18) (all from Peprotech). Co-culture with stromal “feeder” cells (e.g. OP-9) may be recommended to maintain the primary cells (ref), although we did not see an obvious difference in cell growth with or without the feeder cells for specimens we studied.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For scRNA-seq, primary cells were thawed in PBS+5% FBS and treated with DNase I (AMPD1-1KT, Sigma) for 5 min at room temperature. Cells were washed and resuspended with PBS+0.04% BSA. Viability was checked by Trypan Blue (Thermo), and if viability was lower than 95%, live cells were purified by the Dead cell removal kit (MACS). Viable cells were subject to scRNA-seq following the Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 5' v2 protocol. For in vitro Perturb-seq, ells were transduced as described above and maintained in a dish for 9-14 days. For in vivo Perturb-seq, leukemia cells were harvested from BM on day 12 post-transplant. Sorted GFP/mCherry+ leukemia cells were washed 3 times and resuspended in PBS+0.04% BSA and checked for viability. Viable cells were subject to scRNA-seq following the Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 5' v2 protocol with spike-in of sgRNA amplification oligos.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For scRNA-seq, samples were prepared following the Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 5' v2 protocol. For Perturb-seq, samples were subject to the Perturb-seq protocol adapted from ECCITE-seq with small modifications, without antibody-hashtag labelling. Briefly, 2μM sg_RT_v4 (AGCAAGTGAGAAGCATCGTGTCAAAGCACCGACTCGGTGCCAC) oligo was spiked in to the cell suspension containing 20,000 live cells. Cells were barcoded on the 10xGenomics platform following the Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 5' v2 protocol. sgRNA was amplified together with cDNA using a spike-in Guide-tag_additive (AGCAAGTGAGAAGCATCGTGTC), and separated from cDNA by 0.6x SPRIselect beads (Beckman) (beads bind cDNA while supernatant contains sgRNAs). sgRNA was further amplified with primers incorporated with TotalSeq_A_Dual_Index, and purified by 1.2x SPRIselect beads (Beckman). cDNA was amplified and purified following the 10x Genomics protocol. Libraries were analyzed using the Qubit dsDNA HS assay kit (Thermo Fisher) and a High Sensitivity DNA Bioanalyzer Kit (Agilent), and quantified by NEBNext Library Quant Kit for Illumina. Libraries were pooled consisting of 90% cDNA and 10% sgRNA, and pair-end sequenced on a Nova-seq 6000 in Read 1 26, i7 index 10, i5 index 10, Read 2 90bp format.\r\n!Sample_description = in vivo CRISPR screen, day 15 AML drug library, day 14 cas9 virus post-infection\r\n!Sample_data_processing = 10X Cell Ranger (verion 6.1.2) mkfastq for scRNA and sgRNA (if applicable)\r\n!Sample_data_processing = 10X Cell Ranger (verion 6.1.2) mkcount\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38 with GFP and mCherry\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: filtered_feature_bc_matrix from 10X Cell Ranger mkcount\r