  "text": "^SAMPLE = GSM6588400\r\n!Sample_title = DM_CITEseq-1_NA_NM_1 mRNA\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM6588400\r\n!Sample_status = Public on May 23 2023\r\n!Sample_submission_date = Sep 16 2022\r\n!Sample_last_update_date = May 23 2023\r\n!Sample_type = SRA\r\n!Sample_channel_count = 1\r\n!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Npm1c/Flt3ITD leukemia model\r\n!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus\r\n!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sort markers: nomarker\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time point: d0\r\n!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = secondary readout: Antibodies (CITE-seq)\r\n!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cas9-LSK cells were transduced with lentiviral vectors expressing sgRNAs against specific CFs.\r\n!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Primary LSKs were isolated from 12-14 weeks-old ROSA26xCas9 mice and grown ex vivo for 36 hours under Stem Cell conditions (DMEM/F12, ITSX 1X, 1 mg/mL PVA 87%, 10 mM Hepes, 100 ng/uL Tpo, 10 ng/uL SCF). Then, 50,000 viable cells were transplanted to irradiated (902 cGy, 1 minute) 12 weeks-old adult B6.SJL-Ptprca Pepcb/BoyJ (CD45.1) mice via tail injection.\r\n!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = After two weeks, the transplanted mice were euthanised and bone marrow cells were harvested and stained with BV510 anti Lineage (CD3, CD19, Ter119, CD11b, Gr1) and APC anti c-Kit antibodies. For single-cell RNAseq we FACS-sorted Lineage- and Lineage+/cKit+ fractions and processed each of them in a 10X single-cell RNA-seq partition aimed at a final coverage of 500 single-cells per sgRNA.\r\n!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Single-cell libraries were generated using the Chromium Next GEM Single-Cell 3’ Reagent Kits v3.1 (Dual Index) using the 10x Genomics manufacturer recommended protocol and targeting 16,000 cells per library.The resulting libraries were quantified using Qbit and qPCR and analysed on a Tape Station. Libraries were sequenced in a NextSeq 1000 or a Novaseq 6000 to a final coverage of 50,000 reads/cell for 3’ Gene Expression libraries and 5,000 reads/cell for CRISPR Feature Barcode libraries.\r\n!Sample_description = CITE-seq of mouse leukemic model\r\n!Sample_description = DM_CITEseq-1_NA_NM_1.h5\r\n!Sample_description = CellAnnotation_leukemia.tsv\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Raw sequencing data were demultiplexed using the function mkfastq in Cell Ranger (version 6.1.1).\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Sequencing data were aligned to the reference genome with Cell Ranger count\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCm38/mm10 reference genome assembly (GENCODE vM23/Ensembl 98) with BFP and GFP sequences\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: h5 matrices: read count matrix with cells / barcodes (columns) and genes (rows); one for each sample\r\n!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: CellAnnotation: mapping of cell types and other information to barcodes across samples; one for each source (leukemia, in vivo, ex vivo)\r\n!Sample_platform_id = GPL24247\r\n!Sample_contact_name = Brian,,Huntly\r\n!Sample_contact_email = bjph2@cam.ac.uk\r\n!Sample_contact_department = Department of Haematology\r\n!Sample_contact_institute = University of Cambridge\r\n!Sample_contact_address = Hills Road\r\n!Sample_contact_city = Cambridge\r\n!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = CB2 0AW\r\n!Sample_contact_country = United Kingdom\r\n!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000\r\n!Sample_library_selection = cDNA\r\n!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic single cell\r\n!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq\r\n!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN30889638\r\n!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX17605416\r\n!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE213511\r\n!Sample_series_id = GSE213513\r\n!Sample_data_row_count = 0\r\n^SAMPLE = GSM6588401\r\n!Sample_title = DM_CITEseq-1_NA_NM_1 gRNA\r\n!Sample_geo_accession = GSM6588401\r\n!Sample_status